WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.970
Mind your Decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.969
What is the value of the following sum?

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.580
Burger King® asked this problem on Twitter.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:16.080
The value of the sum would be a promo code, that could be used for a free Whopper with any purchase.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.630
To avoid spoiling the answer,

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:24.480
I'm going to solve a slightly different problem to illustrate the method of how you would solve such a problem.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.539
So, what is the value of the following sum:

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:43.300
-Σ(i=1 -&gt; 100) (-1)^i *((5!*5)/4!)^1/2.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:49.900
Pause if you'd like to give this problem a try, and when you're ready, keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.680
So, how can we solve this problem?

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.399
We'll get started by simplifying 5!/4!.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.080
5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1,

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:17.010
and 4! = 4 x 3 x 2 x 1.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:23.160
We can get 5!/4! by dividing 4! from 5!.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:29.620
Notice we'll eliminate 4, 3, 2, &amp; 1 in the product. We're left with just 5.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:36.239
We substitute that in and we have 5 x 5. This will be equal to 5^2.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:42.269
(5^2)^1/2 = 5, so we can then factor out the 5.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:49.709
We then want to evaluate the following sum of (-1)^i, where i = 1 -&gt; 100.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.440
We can write these terms out.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:02:00.760
Now -1^odd num. = -1, and -1^even num. = 1.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.820
We thus simplify the following terms and we have an alternating sum:

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.049
-1+1, and so on and so on until we reach the last pair of -1+1.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:14.428
So, every pair of terms will actually cancel out to be equal to 0.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.320
Therefore this entire sum will be equal to 0, so we have -5  x 0,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.260
and that's, of course, equal to 0.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:28.200
It's great to see a big company use mathematics in its social media promotion.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.320
Let me know if you see any other companies using math in their social media!

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:40.290
Thanks for making Mind your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube. As always, thanks for watching, and thanks for your support.

